{"authored" [{"question" "q-129100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-3,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨7,-2,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,6⟩=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(7,-2,4).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨7,-2,4⟩-⟨8,-3,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,-3,6⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2-3-6|}{\\sqrt{4+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(1,3,4)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-4,2,0⟩=2$, find the shortest distance from $P(5,-2,3)$ to $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,3,4⟩-⟨5,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-4,2,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 0|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|16+10+0|}{\\sqrt{16+4+0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|26|}{\\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "13\\sqrt{20}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "284f654c8be31078dfc2a1fb8c93a519d6a449daa3c295ad90d6e8ab568b029b" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/assets/40ec5f2b2615eedf6b16420a2089b7c377141db46237de35218c5e685b629918.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4949.json" "file_sha256" "2f021ae9e8da5034718eb4af4830369345eccaae8ad409d872f68a72d5f1e472" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(4,8,2).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/assets/0589ebbdb2c14b93e1296b9e1f8b0caa0c3df49bff4c9fbb97e4c18102844ec1.png)\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2+24-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,6\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4949.json" "file_sha256" "2f021ae9e8da5034718eb4af4830369345eccaae8ad409d872f68a72d5f1e472" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(1,-2,-1)$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle = 4,$ find the shortest distance from $P(0 , -1 , 2)$ to $\\Pi.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4950.json" "file_sha256" "d4b188c4a0da07111ace1a3a3770395e7cd1b4e70c295ceebaa28d2b6bb804aa" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-2,-1⟩-⟨0,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+0+6|}{\\sqrt{4+0+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,8\\,|}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4950.json" "file_sha256" "d4b188c4a0da07111ace1a3a3770395e7cd1b4e70c295ceebaa28d2b6bb804aa" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3 , -10 , 3)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation $2x+y-2z = -1$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4951.json" "file_sha256" "7ff97404880265c7c245873147e46cd6a6814b1e097fc7dfc95c75c3f66f6d11" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=4$ and $y=-5$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z & =-1 \\\\ 2(4)+(-5)+1 & =2z \\\\ 4 & =2z \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(4, -5, 2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overrightarrow{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-5,2⟩-⟨3,-10,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle a,b,c \\rangle.$ So, for the plane $\\Pi,$ we have $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 1, -2 \\rangle.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+5+2|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,9\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4951.json" "file_sha256" "7ff97404880265c7c245873147e46cd6a6814b1e097fc7dfc95c75c3f66f6d11" "basis" 1931 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(4,-2,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩=27.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "22ac6626b582e967ddff0270e32d14aa829e4a8bf683e7f0651314c6f0b85872" "basis" 2184 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩ & =27 \\\\ -3x+2y+3z & =27 \\\\ 3z & =27+3x-2y \\\\ z & =9+x-\\frac{2}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=6$ and $y=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=9+6-\\frac{2}{3}(3)=13.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(6,3,13)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨6,3,13⟩-⟨4,-2,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,5,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-3,2,3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+10+18|}{\\sqrt{9+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|22|}{\\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "22ac6626b582e967ddff0270e32d14aa829e4a8bf683e7f0651314c6f0b85872" "basis" 2184 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d72988a0785a347d65bed5dd83fc7047617de8693215da214ff4b79eead2306" "basis" 2184 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear