454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{11}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "22ac6626b582e967ddff0270e32d14aa829e4a8bf683e7f0651314c6f0b85872" "basis" 2184 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{22}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "22ac6626b582e967ddff0270e32d14aa829e4a8bf683e7f0651314c6f0b85872" "basis" 2184 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,5,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-4y+2z=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "22ac6626b582e967ddff0270e32d14aa829e4a8bf683e7f0651314c6f0b85872" "basis" 2184 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-4y+2z & =2 \\\\ 4(1)-4(1)+2z & =2 \\\\ 2z & =2 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,1,1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨-2,5,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-4,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12+16+8|}{\\sqrt{16+16+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|36|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "22ac6626b582e967ddff0270e32d14aa829e4a8bf683e7f0651314c6f0b85872" "basis" 2184 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d72988a0785a347d65bed5dd83fc7047617de8693215da214ff4b79eead2306" "basis" 2184 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/