te.json" "file_sha256" "3b5e409e228f2539e8abc7aa22cd0d248d51b238b3c6e981f9ab2382becc485d" "basis" 2781 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b5e409e228f2539e8abc7aa22cd0d248d51b238b3c6e981f9ab2382becc485d" "basis" 2781 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(5,-1,9)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,-2⟩=3$, find the shortest distance from $P(7,-2,8)$ to $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b5e409e228f2539e8abc7aa22cd0d248d51b238b3c6e981f9ab2382becc485d" "basis" 2781 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,-1,9⟩-⟨7,-2,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨3,-6,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-2)\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6-6-2|}{\\sqrt{9+36+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-14|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{7} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b5e409e228f2539e8abc7aa22cd0d248d51b238b3c6e981f9ab2382becc485d" "basis" 2781 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7df4d0bc75c2dd3c24dfe3a8081d512f07aa13bb766e052b655e431b184d318" "basis" 2781 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b5e409e228f2539e8abc7aa22cd0d248d51b238b3c6e981f9ab2382becc485d" "basis" 2781 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b5e409e228f2539e8abc7aa22cd0d248d51b238b3c6e981f9ab2382becc485d" "basis" 2781 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b5e409e228f2539e8abc7aa22cd0d248d51b238b3c6e981f9ab2382becc485d" "basis" 2781 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b5e409e228f2539e8abc7aa22cd0d248d51b238b3c6e981f9ab2382becc485d" "basis" 2781 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b5e409e228f2539e8abc7aa22cd0d248d51b238b3c6e981f9ab2382becc485d" "basis" 2781 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b5e409e228f2539e8abc7aa22cd0d248d51b238b3c6e981f9ab2382becc485d" "basis" 2781 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-33467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(4,15,-5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(6,9,2).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-5)+(-6)\\cdot 1+7\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-10-6-14|}{\\sqrt{25+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-30|}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-33467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "\\sqrt{30}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{30}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129098" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-4,3,-1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨6,-1,5⟩)\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-2⟩=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129098" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(6,-1,5).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨6,-1,5⟩-⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,-4,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-1,2,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|10\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-10-8-12|}{\\sqrt{1+4+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-30|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{3} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129098" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-129098" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129098" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "\\frac{25}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129098" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-3,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨7,-2,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,6⟩=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(7,-2,4).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨7,-2,4⟩-⟨8,-3,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,-3,6⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2-3-6|}{\\sqrt{4+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(2,0,-5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(6,3,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4+6+18|}{\\sqrt{1+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|28|}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-33451" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33451" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "28"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{14}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{14}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33451" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{14}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(1,2,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(1,-2,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|0\\cdot (-2)+(-4)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4+8|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-129094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,11,1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩=20.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩ & =20 \\\\ 2x-5y+4z & =20 \\\\ 4z & =20-2x+5y \\\\ z & =5-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{4}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=2$ and $y=4,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5-\\frac{1}{2}(2)+\\frac{5}{4}(4)=9.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(2,4,9)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,4,9⟩-⟨-2,11,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-7,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨2,-5,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(4)\\cdot 2+(-7)\\cdot (-5)+8\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|8+35+32|}{\\sqrt{4+25+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|75|}{\\sqrt{45}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" "selection" 