veloper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-129119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(1,3,4)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-4,2,0⟩=2$, find the shortest distance from $P(5,-2,3)$ to $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,3,4⟩-⟨5,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-4,2,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 0|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|16+10+0|}{\\sqrt{16+4+0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|26|}{\\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13\\sqrt{20}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{13}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(4,-2,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩=27.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩ & =27 \\\\ -3x+2y+3z & =27 \\\\ 3z & =27+3x-2y \\\\ z & =9+x-\\frac{2}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=6$ and $y=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=9+6-\\frac{2}{3}(3)=13.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(6,3,13)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨6,3,13⟩-⟨4,-2,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,5,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-3,2,3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+10+18|}{\\sqrt{9+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|22|}{\\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\sqrt{11}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{22}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{22}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(5,-1,9)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,-2⟩=3$, find the shortest distance from $P(7,-2,8)$ to $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,-1,9⟩-⟨7,-2,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨3,-6,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-2)\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6-6-2|}{\\sqrt{9+36+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-14|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{7} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-7,5,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-8y+8z=-36.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-8y+8z & =-36 \\\\ 4(-1)-8(1)+8z & =-36 \\\\ 8z & =-24 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,1,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,1,-3⟩-⟨-7,5,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-4,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-8,8⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-8)+(-5)\\cdot 8|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{8}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|24+32-40|}{\\sqrt{16+64+64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,16\\,|}{\\sqrt{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-80118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,4,-5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-2x+2y+z=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y+z & =6 \\\\ -2(1)+2(1)+z & =6 \\\\ z & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,1,6)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,6⟩-⟨-1,4,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-2,2,1⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 2+11\\cdot 1|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4-6+11|}{\\sqrt{4+4+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-129165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-4,-1,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-4x-2y+2z=16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-2y+2z & =16 \\\\ -4(-1)-2(2)+2z & =16 \\\\ 2z & =16 \\\\ z & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,2,8)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,2,8⟩-⟨-4,-1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,3,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-4,-2,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12-6+6|}{\\sqrt{16+4+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,-12\\,|}{\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-80123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{6}"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{6}"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-80123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,5,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-4y+2z=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-4y+2z & =2 \\\\ 4(1)-4(1)+2z & =2 \\\\ 2z & =2 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,1,1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨-2,5,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-4,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12+16+8|}{\\sqrt{16+16+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|36|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{17}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129158" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,3,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $6x+2y+3z=9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129158" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=0$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+2y+3z & =9 \\\\ 6(1)+2(0)+3z & =9 \\\\ 3z & =3 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,0,1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,0,1⟩-⟨-1,3,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨6,2,3⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot 6+(-3)\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12-6+15|}{\\sqrt{36+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|21|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{7} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129158" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b55cafbc1c1d32aa740aa072423fd697aa57c04e101f4e1487693a3617b4f875"} {"question" "q-129158" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129158" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{30}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "q-129158" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/state.json" "file_sha256" "a53fc91aa36e0f096fe9a0fe1fb66375101d66e05f794c019a3d5bf4fa85c885"} {"question" "e-4949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/assets/40ec5f2b2615eedf6b16420a2089b7c377141db46237de35218c5e685b629918.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/example-4949.json" "file_sha256" "9d140cf6668ce103b72410dc32a9a514157e0004f94d2d9e02752183e228a5e5"} {"question" "e-4949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(4,8,2).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/assets/0589ebbdb2c14b93e1296b9e1f8b0caa0c3df49bff4c9fbb97e4c18102844ec1.png)\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2+24-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,6\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/example-4949.json" "file_sha256" "9d140cf6668ce103b72410dc32a9a514157e0004f94d2d9e02752183e228a5e5"} {"question" "e-4950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(1,-2,-1)$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle = 4,$ find the shortest distance from $P(0 , -1 , 2)$ to $\\Pi.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/example-4950.json" "file_sha256" "d4b188c4a0da07111ace1a3a3770395e7cd1b4e70c295ceebaa28d2b6bb804aa"} {"question" "e-4950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-2,-1⟩-⟨0,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+0+6|}{\\sqrt{4+0+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,8\\,|}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/example-4950.json" "file_sha256" "d4b188c4a0da07111ace1a3a3770395e7cd1b4e70c295ceebaa28d2b6bb804aa"} {"question" "e-4951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3 , -10 , 3)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation $2x+y-2z = -1$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/example-4951.json" "file_sha256" "7ff97404880265c7c245873147e46cd6a6814b1e097fc7dfc95c75c3f66f6d11"} {"question" "e-4951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=4$ and $y=-5$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z & =-1 \\\\ 2(4)+(-5)+1 & =2z \\\\ 4 & =2z \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(4, -5, 2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overrightarrow{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-5,2⟩-⟨3,-10,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle a,b,c \\rangle.$ So, for the plane $\\Pi,$ we have $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 1, -2 \\rangle.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+5+2|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,9\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/example-4951.json" "file_sha256" "7ff97404880265c7c245873147e46cd6a6814b1e097fc7dfc95c75c3f66f6d11"}] "usage" {"e-4950" [] "q-33454" [] "e-4949" [] "q-80049" [] "e-4951" [] "q-129120" [] "q-129163" [] "q-129100" [] "q-80115" []} "basis" 2877 "retractions" [[17592186119580 :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/assets/40ec5f2b2615eedf6b